---
description: TypeScript and code style conventions
globs: "*.{ts,tsx}"
alwaysApply: true
---

- Strict **TypeScript** — no `any`, explicit member accessibility
- No shortened variable names (e.g. `hl` for `highlight`, `btn` for `button`); always use the full word
- **React** + **RxJS** for state management (use `useMachineWard` hook)
- **Luxon** for all date/time formatting
- **4-space indentation**, semicolons required
- **Braces & newlines**: always use curly braces with line breaks for control flow statements (`if`, `for`, `while`, etc.). Do `if (condition) {\n  return;\n}` not `if (condition) return;`
- Minimal JSDocs — code should be self-documenting; refactor if unclear
- No bloated comments, no `TODO:`s (use GitHub issues instead)
- Prefer fewer dependencies; write your own when feasible

- **Accessibility & semantic HTML** — use native semantic elements (`<hr>`, `<button>`, `<nav>`, `<label>`, etc.) over generic `<div>`s; ensure interactive elements have keyboard support and ARIA attributes where needed

### Platform split (`common` / `web` / `mobile`)
- Keep as much logic and state management in `common/` as possible
- `web/` and `mobile/` should focus only on component rendering and platform-specific wiring
- Abstract classes in `common/`, concrete rendering in platform packages
